# Licensing

This repository contains two kinds of material under two different licences.

## Text and derived data — CC BY-SA 4.0

Applies to: `raw/`, `by-chapter/`, `verses.json`, `review_needed.md`

Śārṅgadeva's *Saṅgītaratnākara* (13th century) is itself in the public domain.
The transcription these files derive from is published by **Sanskrit Wikisource**
(https://sa.wikisource.org) under the Creative Commons
Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International licence.

Because these files are a derivative of that transcription, they are
distributed under the same licence:

> Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0)
> https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/

You are free to share and adapt this material, including commercially, provided
you give appropriate credit and distribute any derivative work under the same
licence.

**Attribution:** Sanskrit Wikisource contributors, *सङ्गीतरत्नाकरः*,
https://sa.wikisource.org/wiki/सङ्गीतरत्नाकरः — retrieved 2026-08-17,
CC BY-SA 4.0. Structured, transliterated and segmented in this repository;
see README.md for what the processing does and does not change.

The Sanskrit text itself has not been emended. Where the source is ambiguous or
internally inconsistent, the reading is preserved and the problem recorded in
`review_needed.md` rather than corrected.

